{"availability":"available","full":"nesquena/steward-os","name":"steward-os","description":"StewardOS - agentic autonomous OSS system","category":"Developer tools","language":"Ruby","stars":71,"forks":8,"created":"2026-06-19T22:37:15Z","updated":"2026-10-06T23:25:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nesquena.github.io/steward-os/","topics":["ai-agents","maintainer-tools","open-source"],"demo":"https://nesquena.github.io/steward-os/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:45.981Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:45.981Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:45.981Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:45.981Z","stars":71,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An operating model for running a software project with an AI agent as a genuine co-maintainer.","Steward is not an application. It is a system — a set of playbooks, skills, and processes that let you drop an agent (or a team of agents) into any software project and have it help triage issues, review and merge pull requests, run quality gates, talk to your community, and keep the whole machine healthy — at a level of rigor that holds up in a real open-source project.","It is project-agnostic by design. Nothing here is specific to any one codebase. You bring the project; Steward brings the operating model, the recipes, and the questions it needs to ask you to wire itself up."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nesquena/steward-os/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f18e8b2016e21b22c96b245762259d8f98dae556946c8a98e45358fafc40b88b","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:46.117Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:46.117Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An operating model for running a software project with an AI agent as a genuine co-maintainer.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nesquena/steward-os/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f18e8b2016e21b22c96b2457622